    "lawCode": "Amd §21, Chap 644 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Judiciary",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1728\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend chapter 644 of the laws of 2008,\namending the general obligations law relating to powers of attorney,\nin relation to delaying the effective date thereof\n\n PURPOSE OF BILL : This bill enacts a chapter amendment to Assembly\nbill A.6421-B, Chapter 644 of the laws of 2008 changing the enactment\ndate from March 1, 2009 to September 1, 2009.\n\n JUSTIFICATION : Assembly bill A.6421-B, Chapter 644 of the laws of\n2008 was signed into law on 1/27/09 with an enactment date of March 1,\n2009. Since A.6421-B provides a comprehensive change in the law\nregarding power of attorney requirements, additional time is needed to\neducate the legal community regarding this change. Therefore, the\nenactment date is changed to September 1, 2009.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY : New Bill, 2009 - Chapter Amendment to Ch. 644\n'08.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :  None.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE : Immediately.\n",
